      "created" : "2018-01-20T11:33:36.554-0500",
      "creator" : {
         "accountId" : "557058:4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
         "accountType" : "atlassian",
         "active" : true,
         "avatarUrls" : {
            "16x16" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "24x24" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "32x32" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "48x48" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png"
         },
         "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
         "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
         "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
      },
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i003x3:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I think this is working correctly for 'localtime' which is what matters most. I think that's all thats provided by the builtin standard time code in locales.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "But it would be nice to be able to construct a timezone object for an arbitrary timezone, and have that work too.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "REview TimeZoneInformationType  code. It maybe needs to be enahnced to include the rules from the TZDatabase.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe use tzdatabase (somehow compiled/parsed). Maybe find stdc way of doing it. Maybe use boost. But somehow make it easy to say Timezone tz= “America/NewYork” or some such.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "\tLook at using ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/libs/locale/doc/html/dates_times_timezones.html"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "http://www.boost.org/doc/libs/1_52_0/libs/locale/doc/html/dates_times_timezones.html",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : " boost::locale::calendar - to ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I read the code that comes with the TZDatabase. It looks like everthing is there to do what I want, but its a mess, and appears hardwired to work for the current timezone from an environment variable. I would need to significantly adapt that code to make it work in stroika for abitrary handed in tz.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Maybe thats what ICU or boost does?",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Another note on this:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "*",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "@todo   MAYBE use ",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              },
                              {
                                 "marks" : [
                                    {
                                       "attrs" : {
                                          "href" : "http://www.iana.org/time-zones/repository/releases/tzdata2015b.tar.gz"
                                       },
                                       "type" : "link"
                                    }
                                 ],
                                 "text" : "http://www.iana.org/time-zones/repository/releases/tzdata2015b.tar.gz",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              },
                              {
                                 "text" : " and code - and have part of",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "thirdpartylibs, and then compile the zone file there, and reference that somehow here? Or add something",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "to that code to generate our own table which we can #include? Maybe add BuildTools (like Tools) - and",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "there no dependnecies on stroika (execept makefile part) - and build code which we use to boostrap stroika",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  },
                  {
                     "content" : [
                        {
                           "content" : [
                              {
                                 "text" : "building file in intermediatefiles which we #incldue as initailzied data for timezone module",
                                 "type" : "text"
                              }
                           ],
                           "type" : "paragraph"
                        }
                     ],
                     "type" : "listItem"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "bulletList"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "AND - when I do this - add checks to Test_9_TZOffsetAndDaylightSavingsTime_ () also use explicit timezones.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
